        >>[x] Read an entity's notes across active and archive areas =notes-read $One Core/adapter read returns an entity's notes from every sidecar, active and archive, each read once. Done: tests built with the real `clearhead archive charter` cover an archived action, a closed action, a charter with a Habits file, and no duplicates. Unparsable sidecars (active or archive) become sidecar-corrupt findings and are skipped, never silently; I/O errors fail (Darrion, 2026-11-16). PROGRESS 2026-11-20 (Darrion + facilitator): DECIDED the read mirrors append, a pure Core half plus a filesystem adapter half (hover needs the pure half, since the server holds its data). Uncommitted in clearhead-core: sidecar::notes_for(metadata, entity) -> &\[Note], one entity's notes in one sidecar; still needs its doc comment fixed (it says 'entire charter') and a test (two appends read back in order, unknown id gives empty). NEXT: decide the multi-sidecar pure function's input, raw (path, text) pairs or pre-parsed CharterMetadata; output is notes sorted by at plus sidecar-corrupt findings. Then the adapter's list of active and archive sidecar paths (open question: does archive charter carry .habits.actions? archive_charter.rs:31 omits it). DONE 2026-11-23 (Darrion + Claude, Core 8b37def, 180ca85, daf81e3): pure half sidecar::notes_for and notes_across (sorted by at, ties keep input order) over parsed CharterMetadata; assembly parses each sidecar once into WorkspaceRead.sidecars (replacing the active-only notes union and merge_notes), every unparsable sidecar is a sidecar-corrupt finding. Archive is read only when asked: ReadScope::WithArchive in plan_workspace_read reads archive/.<uuid>.json, exposed as filesystem::read_workspace_with_archive; read_workspace stays active-only (Darrion: minimize read cost for the 90%). archive charter does carry .habits.actions; its doc was stale.$ +steward ^2026-11-16T21:49 %2026-11-23T22:37 #01a1e655-cea0-7f02-876c-19390fe96188
        >>[x] Show an entity's notes in the CLI =notes-show $Add --json to show action and show charter carrying the entity's notes, and a Notes section in their text output, via =notes-read. DONE (Core 6c5539f): show action and show charter resolve live entities, closed ones included; archived entities are read with show notes.$ +steward ^2026-11-16T21:49 %2026-11-24T06:45 <notes-read #01a1e655-cec4-7621-bef5-9a51af089de2
        >>[ ] List notes in LSP hover =notes-hover $Hover lists an action's notes from data the server already holds, with no full read per hover.$ +steward ^2026-11-16T21:49 <notes-read #01a1e655-cee4-78a2-88a7-df2cc5d34892
    >[x] jot appends to the sidecar and takes any entity id =notes-jot $No new verb. jot writes a note {at, by, text} to the sidecar of the entity's charter, accepting a charter, action or Habit id; no longer appends to ## Log. by comes from the writer's identity. Done includes updating the clearhead skill's 'Keep actions readable' section to send action history to the action's own notes.$ +steward ^2026-11-09T02:11 %2026-11-24T07:26 <notes-render #01a1be13-34b2-7891-9644-b8a80e44f6b2
